I haven't died post quest with a wizard for a long time. I get careless 
in other ways. I play elven wizards btw.

You can have metal helm and boots and it only gets you 3% failure rate 
for combat spells. Use your pet. Change to dagger and practice it 
against easy foes. I name the first non cursed elven dagger Sting and 
use it. Quiver other daggers and start throwing them. Sacrifice on first 
altar to get the magicbane. Use two uncursed scrolls of enchant weapon 
for the magigbane and the blessed ones for the quivered daggers. When 
you get the magicbane *use it*, I mean athame does not dull when engraving.

Try not to be burdened and never more encumbered than that. (OK, there 
is one exception that can be safe.) If you are burdened be ready to drop 
what is encumbering you the minute you see danger. Throw your daggers 
first, don't use the force bolt as it shatters potions, give the final 
blow with the wielded weapon. Sting let's you see o's, you can lure them 
one at a time in most cases, but luring them in straight passage and let 
them have it with magic missiles and throw daggers is just fun. half of 
them will die when the ones in back return your daggers.

